    "symbolReading": "The Hermit stands alone on a snowy summit, his grey cloak a mark of humility — the truly wise need no ornament. The lantern he lifts holds a six-pointed star, the inner divine light. The staff in his left hand is the weight of past experience, keeping him balanced on rough ground. He faces left, towards the unconscious: his search goes inward, not outward. The solitude of the peak isn't punishment but choice — to see more clearly, you sometimes have to stand higher.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The Hermit corresponds to Jung's Sage archetype, the deep wisdom that comes through solitude and reflection. In Albedo, the soul needs to step back from the group in order to hear its own voice. Water Violet people carry a natural, elegant distance — it isn't that they dislike people, but that they need more time alone. The challenge is not letting that independence harden into isolation.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When you keep your distance by habit and feel out of place in company, Water Violet keeps you company as you hold your independence and still let warm connection come in.",
    "step1Status": "You may not share much about yourself and would rather digest a difficulty alone. Others see you as independent and graceful, and sometimes, late at night, the quiet is too quiet — you simply don't know how to begin.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to feel accompanied even in solitude",
