    "keywords": "Fairness, decision, transition, boundary, threshold",
    "uprightMessage": "You are in an important transition — changing work, moving house, ending a relationship, or beginning a new chapter. A clear decision is needed, and it has to rest on honesty. Ask yourself: what is genuinely fair here? Not only to others, but to you.",
    "reversedReminder": "Are you too easily moved by other people's opinions in this transition? Voices around you have you revising and re-revising, and what you'd finally settled gets unsettled again. Protecting your own decision isn't selfish; it's the boundary you most need right now.",
    "symbolReading": "Justice sits between two pillars, echoing the High Priestess and the Hierophant. In her right hand the sword points up — clear discernment; in her left, the scales weigh cause and effect. The red robe is the resolve to act; the green edge of the cloak is the possibility of growth. The square jewel in her crown marks the steadiness of reason. Her feet are hidden inside her robe, hinting that justice rests not only on logic but on the unseen, intuitive, bodily knowing.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The judging archetype represents the inner arbiter — the faculty that helps us choose in line with the soul at life's crossroads. Albedo is a purifying stage that asks you to see clearly what stays and what goes. Walnut protects the boundary of transition: when you're changing form, old ties and outside expectations pull hardest. Jung called this the threshold experience; crossing it takes not only courage but clarity.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When you're in a period of change and easily shaken by people and circumstances, Walnut keeps you company as your inner boundary firms, protecting your new direction through the crossing.",
    "step1Status": "You may be going through a major change; you'd made up your mind, and then one comment from someone left you hesitating. You take in other people's feelings and views easily, and in a vulnerable transition the interference makes holding your direction hard.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to protect my decision through the change",
    "step3Body": "Notice the outer line of your arms — the path of defensive qi from shoulder to the back of the hand. With your other hand, stroke lightly from shoulder to fingertips, as if drawing yourself a boundary.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, imagine a clear shell of light descending from your crown and covering you; breathing out, feel it grow more solid, the noise outside kept outside. Four rounds.",
    "aromaGuide": "Before going out, dab MUNI ONE oil on your wrists and behind your ears, so the scent is a boundary you carry — your own frequency held in a crowd.",
    "dailyPractice": "When someone offers you advice today, pause for five seconds before answering. Put a hand on your lower belly and ask: is this my feeling, or theirs? Then reply.",
    "awarenessNote": "Awareness is like a crab that has just moulted. Of course you're especially sensitive while the new shell is still soft — that isn't weakness, it's proof you're growing. Find a safe place to stay until it hardens.",
