    "uprightMessage": "You feel hung upside down in mid-air, able to do nothing — and it's precisely this stillness that shows you an angle you'd normally miss. Not every wait is wasted time; sometimes the deepest transformation happens while you don't move at all. Let yourself hang here. The clouds will drift in from another direction.",
    "reversedReminder": "A heaviness you can't explain has settled around you — no cause, no trigger, it simply arrived. You've tried to think your way out, tried to rally, and this isn't something willpower solves. This feeling doesn't need explaining. It only needs to be seen.",
    "symbolReading": "The Hanged Man hangs from a living T-shaped tree, hands bound behind him — and his face is calm, a golden halo around his head. His right foot is tied; his left crosses into the shape of a 4. Action is suspended; consciousness is free. The inverted view shows him a landscape he could never see standing up. Red trousers are the passion still present, the blue tunic spiritual awareness. This isn't punishment — it's a pause he chose.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The Sacrificed God represents the ego's voluntary letting-go in Jung's individuation — not passive victimhood but active surrender. Albedo asks for the courage to do nothing. Mustard corresponds to the sudden deep gloom that arrives for no reason, like a cloud drifting in without a sound. Jung held that this nameless darkness is often the signal of a major reorganisation happening in the unconscious.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When a deep, causeless low settles over you like a sudden cloud, Mustard keeps you company as you hold faith in the dark and wait for the moment the cloud disperses on its own.",
    "step1Status": "You may wake one day and find everything grey with no reason attached. Work is fine, relationships haven't changed, and a deep, heavy something is pressing on your chest. You suspect that even saying it wouldn't be understood.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow the low to visit; it will leave by itself",
    "step3Body": "Notice your head and neck — does your head feel especially heavy, your neck barely holding it? Let your head hang gently forward and feel the back of the neck lengthening.",
    "breathing": "Lie face down on a bed or mat (head turned to a comfortable position) and feel your belly press into the surface as you breathe. Let gravity do the relaxing. Three minutes.",
    "aromaGuide": "At the greyest moment, put MUNI ONE oil on a hot towel and lay it over your forehead. Eyes closed, let warmth and scent seep in like sunlight through cloud.",
