    "dailyPractice": "Stand in front of a mirror for three minutes today, looking at your face without judging or adjusting it. If a critical thought arises, simply notice it, and say quietly to your reflection: \"You're fine as you are.\"",
    "awarenessNote": "Awareness is like an old craftsman restoring an antique. A crack isn't a defect — it's filled with gold lacquer and becomes the object's most distinctive line. Every mark on you is evidence that you have lived.",
