    "uprightMessage": "Something is coming down — a relationship, a belief, or a way of life you thought was solid. It hurts; your world has been turned over. But the lightning strikes only the structures that are no longer true, and your real foundation is deeper than you knew. In the rubble you'll find what was buried and what actually matters.",
    "reversedReminder": "The shocking event may be some time behind you, and your body seems still to be in that moment. A sudden noise makes you jump; certain images arrive uninvited. Your body remembers, and that's how it protects you. You can tell it slowly: it's safe now.",
    "symbolReading": "Lightning strikes the crown at the tower's top, flames burst from the windows, two figures fall from a height. The tower is built on rock — the foundation holds; what collapses is everything added on top. The crown blasted away is the shattering of a false sense of control. Twenty-two flames (one for each Major Arcanum) fall from the sky: this destruction is a total awakening. The falling figures have finally left the tower that held them — a hard landing, and they are free.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "Destruction and revelation are what Jung called the crisis of individuation — when the old ego structure can no longer carry the soul's growth, it is blown open from inside. The yellowing fire of Citrinitas burns the Persona and false security. Star of Bethlehem corresponds to the shocked state after trauma, the dazed condition of being broken open by impact. Jung held that this collapse, though painful, is the necessary road to the Self breaking through.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When a sudden shock has left body and mind stunned and dazed, Star of Bethlehem keeps you company as steady breath is found in the rubble, and the shattered pieces slowly gather again.",
    "step1Status": "You may have been through something abrupt — an accident, a break-up, a job lost, serious bad news. The world seems to have cracked open, and everything you thought certain has turned uncertain. You may still be in shock; it may not feel entirely real.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow the old structure to fall, making room for who I really am",
    "step3Body": "Notice your heartbeat and breath — are they faster than usual? Cross your arms over your chest and tap alternately left and right like butterfly wings, breathing out slowly as you tap.",
    "breathing": "In for four, as if picking up a fragment; hold for two, setting it in place; out for six, letting the body remember: I am still here. Eight rounds of this settling breath.",
    "aromaGuide": "Apply MUNI ONE oil generously to your inner wrists and hold them near your nose, using smell to build a sensory anchor for now, this moment, safe.",
