    "dailyPractice": "Go out and look at the stars tonight (or look properly at a photo of a night sky for three minutes). Pick the one that seems brightest and imagine it's shining for you. Tomorrow, check whether it's still there. It will be.",
    "awarenessNote": "Awareness is like a cactus flowering in the desert — in the least likely place, life finds its way. You don't have to wait until you're in a garden to bloom. You already are; you just haven't noticed.",
