    "jungianAnalysis": "The Divine Child appears near the completion of individuation — the innocent core self, uncontaminated by the world. Rubedo is alchemy's final integration, where fire and spirit fuse to produce the philosopher's gold. Honeysuckle people project that golden light onto the past rather than the present — their happy memories are so beautiful that now looks dim by comparison. Jung reminds us that the Divine Child always lives in this moment, never in recollection.",
