    "jungianAnalysis": "The World corresponds to Jung's Self — the final aim of individuation, the complete integration of consciousness and the unconscious. Rubedo's last crystal is the philosopher's stone, a total sense of wholeness. What Larch people lack isn't ability but confidence — they assume failure before setting out, and so never take the first step. The World says: you are already whole; nothing more needs waiting for. Jung's final wisdom is that the Self isn't a place you arrive at — it's the place you've always been.",
