    "keywords": "Choice, direction, vision, the crossroads, inner compass",
    "uprightMessage": "You're at a fork in the road, holding two possibilities. This isn't a question of right and wrong but of who you'd rather become. You don't have to decide now — and don't let hesitation turn into avoidance. Something in you already knows the direction; it just needs a little courage to be admitted.",
    "reversedReminder": "When you swing back and forth, the question usually isn't \"which is better\" but \"what am I afraid of\". The thing making you hesitate may be exactly the direction worth moving towards.",
    "symbolReading": "The figure in the Two of Wands stands on a battlement, a staff in one hand and a globe in the other, gazing into the distance. He already has something, and he knows a larger world is waiting. The two wands are two options, two roads. The wall is known safety; the distance is an unknown calling. This card isn't about leaving — it's about deciding where you want to go.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Two is opposition and choice, and in fire it appears as will splitting and reintegrating. When a creative impulse meets two directions, the ego must make its first conscious decision. This is early individuation — moving from unconscious impulse to conscious choosing. The lesson of the Two is that choice isn't a limitation but the way power gets concentrated.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Scleranthus people swing like a pendulum between two options, this one good one moment and the other right the next. This flower's wisdom is helping you find your inner balance point — the centre that can settle without anyone else's opinion.",
    "step1Status": "You may be hesitating between two decent options, or swinging between known comfort and unknown possibility. Notice whether you keep gathering more information in order to postpone deciding.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to trust the direction my heart already knows",
    "step3Body": "Stand up and shift your weight from the left foot to the right, then back to the middle. The moment when both feet bear weight evenly is your centre.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, imagine one option in each hand; breathing out, bring the palms together at your chest. Seven times, feeling the stillness inside.",
    "aromaGuide": "Lavender with lemon — the lavender eases the anxiety of deciding, the lemon brings clarity of judgement, helping you see through the fog to the direction.",
    "dailyPractice": "When a choice arises today, give yourself three deep breaths and ask: \"If I weren't afraid of getting it wrong, which would I choose?\" Use that answer as your clue.",
    "awarenessNote": "Hesitation is like standing between two boats with a foot in each — the further they drift apart, the less steady you are. Choosing isn't finding the perfect answer; it's deciding to stand firmly in one boat and then giving everything to sail it where you want to go.",
    "systemL1": "Scleranthus",
