    "keywords": "Celebration, belonging, honest joy, safety, milestone",
    "uprightMessage": "This is a moment worth celebrating; you've reached a small milestone. But real celebration isn't a smile performed for others — it's the quiet satisfaction inside: I did this, and I did it as myself. Let yourself feel that fully, at full strength.",
    "reversedReminder": "If a celebration makes you uneasy, or you're smiling while something else is happening inside, that's a valuable signal. You don't have to look happy all the time.",
    "symbolReading": "The Four of Wands shows a flower canopy made from four staffs, with people celebrating beneath it. The canopy means a stable structure has formed — not temporary, but solid. The castle in the distance is a foundation already built. The most important image, though, is the garlands and the genuine smiles: celebration isn't about the display, it's about whether you actually let yourself be happy.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Four is stability and structure, and in fire it appears as passion finding a safe container. Four is the first complete frame — four directions, four walls, a home. In individuation, four marks the first integration of personality: you begin to have a place that is yours. But fire's four also warns that stability mustn't harden, and joy only means something when it's real.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Agrimony people always carry a smile, covering unease and pain with humour and optimism. This flower's healing is in knowing that you don't have to appear happy to deserve love. Being able to tell someone you trust \"actually, today has been hard\" is the real courage.",
    "step1Status": "You may be in a situation that looks like it should be joyful and something feels off. Or you may answer everything with a smile, even when that isn't the whole truth. Notice whether you use \"I'm fine\" to answer concern.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow real feeling a place even inside celebration",
    "step3Body": "Put both hands on your cheeks and feel the expression on your face right now. Don't adjust it, just observe — what is your face saying?",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, lift the corners of your mouth slightly; breathing out, release every muscle in the face completely. Eight times, feeling the ease of a smile that costs nothing.",
    "aromaGuide": "Geranium with petitgrain — the geranium opens the heart so feeling can move, the petitgrain eases the tension hidden behind the smile.",
    "dailyPractice": "Find a moment alone today and say aloud three things you actually feel right now — pleasant or not. You don't have to solve them; just let yourself hear them.",
    "awarenessNote": "Real celebration is like a tree flowering in spring. It doesn't bloom to be admired — the season came, the nourishment was there, and it opened. If joy takes great effort, perhaps what you need isn't more celebration but better care of the soil around the roots.",
