    "keywords": "Victory, recognition, confidence, after the applause, inner light",
    "uprightMessage": "You did it, and it was seen. That recognition is warm — enjoy it. And remember that what carried you here wasn't the applause but the days you kept going when nobody was watching. Today's acknowledgement is a bonus. Your worth has never needed anyone else to define it.",
    "reversedReminder": "If you find you need praise to feel all right, it may mean you don't yet truly believe in your own capability. Next time you're praised, try letting that warmth be stored inside.",
    "symbolReading": "In the Six of Wands a rider wearing a laurel crown moves through a crowd on a white horse, a laurel tied to the staff in his hand as well. People cheer on both sides. What's most worth noticing is his bearing — not display, but steadiness. The white horse is unclouded will. The card reminds us that a real victor doesn't need to announce it, because their presence is already a kind of light.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Six is harmony and return, and in fire it appears as balance between personal will and collective recognition. Six answers the conflict of five — integration achieved through friction. But fire's six has a subtle trap: build your worth entirely on outside recognition and the silence after applause will feel like emptiness. The real work of six is finding the inner laurel.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Heather people long to be noticed and heard, talk a great deal, and want the conversation to circle back to them. Beneath that longing is deep loneliness — a fear that if they aren't noticeable they'll be forgotten. This flower helps you discover that in your quiet, you are still seen.",
    "step1Status": "You may have just received recognition or achieved something, and found the pleasure less lasting than you expected. Or you may be longing for one particular person's approval. Notice where that sense of \"not enough\" comes from.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to admire my own light, quietly",
    "step3Body": "Put a hand on your heart and say softly: \"You did well.\" Notice whether something in the chest opens a little.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, imagine warm golden light entering through the crown; breathing out, let it spread outward from your heart. Five times, letting the light be your own.",
    "aromaGuide": "Frankincense with neroli — the frankincense brings a settled confidence, the neroli comforts the child inside who still feels uneasy amid applause.",
    "dailyPractice": "Spend a minute in front of a mirror looking into your own eyes without speaking. Then say three things you've been proud of lately. Don't add \"it's nothing\" — let the acknowledgement land completely.",
    "awarenessNote": "Applause is like an echo. It rings around the valley for a while and then goes quiet. If your confidence is built on the echo, every silence will alarm you. If your confidence is the mountain itself, you can enjoy the echo and not fear its ending.",
