    "uprightMessage": "Someone is challenging your position — openly, or through silent pressure. What's needed now isn't attack but standing firmly, like a tree: not chasing the wind, only rooting deeper. You have the right to protect what matters to you.",
    "reversedReminder": "If you find yourself always giving way — not because you agree, but because conflict is uncomfortable — that's worth noticing. Sometimes your silence isn't kindness; it's overlooking yourself.",
    "symbolReading": "In the Seven of Wands one figure stands on high ground, alone against six staffs coming up at him, fending them off one by one. He wears mismatched shoes — the situation arrived suddenly, without preparation. His stance is firm and strong, not because he isn't afraid but because he knows what he's guarding. The card says you don't have to be perfect to be entitled to defend your ground.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Seven is inner testing and refinement, and in fire it appears as the true quality of will under pressure. Seven is a sacred number, marking spiritual trial. Your boundary is being tested, and the point of that test isn't winning but discovering whether your core values still stand under strain. It's a key moment of integration.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Centaury people are kind and gentle and find refusal very hard, even when the requests exhaust them. This flower's strength is helping you find a way to refuse that is gentle and firm at once — you can say no and still be the kind person you are.",
    "step1Status": "You may be carrying pressure or expectation from others while a voice inside wants to say no and can't. Notice whether you use accommodation to avoid an uncomfortable feeling.",
