    "dailyPractice": "Practise one gentle refusal today. When someone asks something you'd rather not agree to, say \"let me think about it\" — give yourself time to feel what you actually want, then answer in your own way.",
    "awarenessNote": "A boundary isn't a high wall keeping everyone out — it's more like the fence around a garden, with a gate you can open or close. The point isn't to keep the gate shut forever, but that the choice stays in your hands rather than someone else's.",
