    "keywords": "Gathering, friendship, sharing, celebrating together, warmth without imposing",
    "uprightMessage": "This is a time for shared joy — celebrating, laughing and raising a glass with people you trust. Friendship is one of life's most precious gifts, and it needs no special reason to gather. Let your happiness travel naturally to the people around you — and let each of them feel it in their own way.",
    "reversedReminder": "Your enthusiasm for something may be quietly becoming pressure — you want too much for others to be as excited as you are. Everyone runs at a different temperature; letting someone celebrate quietly is also respect.",
    "symbolReading": "In the Three of Cups three women raise their cups, dancing in a place abundant with flowers and fruit. Harvest and garlands lie at their feet. Three figures form a stable triangle — the strongest social structure, more resilient than a pair. The fruit is what they have grown together. The card reminds us that joy amplifies when it's shared, as long as everyone is enjoying it freely.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Three is creation and synthesis, and in water it appears as feeling expressed and shared outwardly. Three is the first number beyond duality — a relationship of two takes in a third (a friend, a community, a child), and feeling begins to expand. Water's three brings the joy of belonging, and one piece of work: is your enthusiasm inviting or imposing? Real connection lets everyone keep their own tempo.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Vervain people are full of passion and ideals, convinced that what they've found should be known by everyone. That fervour is beautiful and can slip into preaching. This flower helps you learn to share your light and let people decide for themselves whether to step into it.",
    "step1Status": "You may be in a socially energised period with much you want to share. Notice whether your enthusiasm is missing what the other person actually feels, or whether \"we should all be happy\" is overriding a different voice.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow everyone to feel joy in their own way",
    "step3Body": "Reach out your arms as though to hug someone, then draw them back around yourself. Hug yourself first, then bring that warmth to others. Notice the difference between the two.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, open your arms to the world; breathing out, bring your hands back to your heart. Five times, feeling the rhythm of opening and gathering.",
    "aromaGuide": "Grapefruit with lavender — the grapefruit brings social ease and pleasure, the lavender reminds you to keep an inner quiet inside the noise.",
    "dailyPractice": "Invite a friend for a drink or a walk today, and practise spending half the time listening. Not waiting for your turn — genuinely curious: \"And then what? How did that feel?\"",
    "awarenessNote": "Sharing joy is like passing a torch: lighting someone else's doesn't diminish your own flame. But pushing the torch into the hands of someone who doesn't want it isn't sharing, it's forcing. The best sharing lets your light fall naturally around you, and whoever wants to come closer will.",
    "systemL1": "Vervain",
    "systemL2Echo": "Page of Wands",
    "systemEmotionGroup": "Over-care for others",
    "systemMeridian": "Triple Burner channel (shaoyang; ministerial fire running too high)",
    "systemExtraordinary": "Yang Wei vessel (linking)",
    "systemAlchemy": "Albedo (the whitening)",
    "systemQiFlow": "The ministerial fire floating loose, pushing at others"
