    "bachGroup": "Uncertainty",
    "alchemyStage": "Citrinitas (the yellowing)",
    "keywords": "Illusion, choice, the inner voice, temptation, telling true from false",
    "uprightMessage": "A great many tempting options have appeared, each of them glittering. Not everything that shines is gold. What you need now isn't more outside advice but quiet enough to hear your own heart — among all the options, which one brings calm rather than excitement? That's your answer.",
    "reversedReminder": "If you keep asking for opinions and none of the advice feels right, it's because you already have the answer and daren't trust it. Others can see your surface; only you can hear what's at the bottom of you.",
    "symbolReading": "The Seven of Cups is one of the most dreamlike images in tarot — a silhouette faces seven cups floating in cloud, each holding something different: a castle, jewels, a laurel, a snake, a dragon, a veiled face, a glowing figure. A mixture of desire, fear and fantasy. The clouds mean these options aren't real; they are your own projections. The card says: before choosing, tell apart what you truly want from what you think you want.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Seven is spiritual testing and awakening, and in water it appears as a labyrinth of feeling. Seven is a spiritual number; it doesn't hand you an answer but tests whether you can stay clear inside illusion. This is another form of facing the shadow — among these attractive options, some are genuine longing and some are mirages projected by unmet lack. Telling them apart is your work now.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Cerato people lack confidence in their own judgement, asking one person and then another and ending up more confused. This flower's gift is reconnecting you with intuition — the inner voice that knew the answer before you started thinking.",
    "step1Status": "You may be dazzled by too many options or temptations, or seeking outside advice and getting more lost. Notice whether \"let me look a bit longer\" is delaying a decision you've already made inside.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to trust intuition over outside advice",
    "step3Body": "Close your eyes and put your attention in your belly, not your head. Ask yourself the question you're hesitating over, and notice whether the belly tightens or softens. Tight is no, soft is yes.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, imagine all the tangled options floating in front of you like bubbles; breathing out, blow them gently away, leaving only the clearest one. Five times, until the picture is clear.",
    "aromaGuide": "Sage with frankincense — the sage clears tangled thinking like wind through fog, the frankincense connects deep intuition so the truth can surface.",
    "dailyPractice": "When a decision comes up today, sit quietly for three minutes before asking anyone. Hand on your heart, ask: \"If I already knew the answer, what would it be?\" Write down the first thing that surfaces.",
    "awarenessNote": "Your intuition is like a radio always playing the right station — but with too many radios on at once you can't hear any of them. Other people's advice is those other stations: not bad, just interference. Sometimes the best thing is to switch everything else off, and in the quiet you'll hear your own frequency.",
    "systemL1": "Cerato",
    "systemL2Echo": "I",
    "systemEmotionGroup": "Uncertainty",
    "systemMeridian": "Spleen channel (taiyin damp earth; governs thought)",
    "systemExtraordinary": "Dai vessel (belt)",
    "systemAlchemy": "Citrinitas (the yellowing)",
    "systemQiFlow": "The centre without a ruler, scattering outward for help"
