    "uprightMessage": "You're the one still seated at the prow in the storm — not because you don't fear the waves but because you've learned to balance inside them. In your hands, feeling isn't a flood but a river, and you can guide it where it's needed. That maturity is the finest medal the years have given you.",
    "reversedReminder": "Do you find yourself always talking, always sharing, always seeking a response? That hand reaching outward may be there because there's an inner space you daren't sit in alone. Try sitting a while in silence and hearing what's in it.",
    "symbolReading": "The King sits on a stone throne surrounded by heaving sea, and not a drop touches the hem of his robe. A cup in one hand and a sceptre in the other: feeling and will in balance. A fish and a small ship appear at his feet, marking his presence in both conscious and unconscious worlds. Air within water lets him turn deep feeling into language and connection.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The master of feeling shows the capacity to navigate an inner ocean — the quietest presence in the eye of the storm. His shadow is Heather's over-talking, filling every silence with speech for fear of sinking into his own depths alone. The path of individuation is becoming self-sufficient in solitude, so silence becomes another kind of fullness.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When you constantly need someone to talk to, can't close the conversation, and feel empty and panicky alone, Heather keeps you company on the way back from the noise, to discover how rich your own company already is.",
    "step1Status": "You may be steering conversations towards your own story without noticing, or being over-lively in company to avoid being alone, with a phone full of messages still to send and replies still to wait for.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow silence to exist; it doesn't mean being forgotten.",
    "step3Body": "Notice your throat. When you're rushing to speak it can tighten and lift — swallow once, let the jaw soften, and allow the next three seconds to be breath only.",
    "breathing": "In for four in silence, hold for two feeling the weight of the quiet, out for six in silence. Five rounds in complete stillness, letting the silence be a gift.",
