    "keywords": "Truth, clarity, clearing the mind, the double-edged blade, the power of discernment",
    "uprightMessage": "A clear insight is cutting through your fog — you're finally seeing something you didn't want to face. This sword has two edges: it can remove what's no longer needed and leave you lighter, and it can wound you and others. Choose to use the truth to purify rather than to attack.",
    "reversedReminder": "If you're holding yourself or someone else to a severe standard, remember: clarity and harshness aren't the same. You can see imperfection without needing to reject yourself or anyone for it.",
    "symbolReading": "In the Ace of Swords a hand emerges from cloud holding an upright blade, its point through a golden crown hung with olive and palm. The sword is the mind's edge; the crown is the authority that clarity brings. Most telling is the cloud — truth arrives from beyond personal thinking. The olive is peace, the palm is victory: the greatest victory is using truth to bring peace rather than to make more conflict.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The energy of the Ace is a pure beginning, and in air it appears as the mind's first light — the instant consciousness is born from chaos, a thought clear as lightning splitting a formerly blurred sky. Air's Ace carries a danger too: pure reason without the heart's warmth becomes cold judgement. The card asks you to bring compassion along when you use the mind's power.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "Crab Apple people carry a deep unease about impurity and imperfection, possibly over-attentive to an outer blemish or an inner uncleanness. This flower's wisdom is helping you understand that purification isn't removing everything you dislike, but seeing with a wider eye that what you call a flaw is also part of your whole.",
    "step1Status": "You may have just seen a truth that doesn't sit comfortably — about yourself, someone else, or a situation. Notice whether the clarity is turning into excessive criticism, or whether you're examining under a magnifying glass something you could actually accept.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow the truth to purify rather than to negate me",
    "step3Body": "Rub your palms warm and rest them gently over your eyes. Feel the eyes soften in that darkness. When you take your hands away and open them, the world will look clearer.",
    "breathing": "Breathing in, imagine white light entering through the crown and washing your thinking; breathing out, imagine every muddy thought leaving as grey smoke. Seven times.",
    "aromaGuide": "Tea tree with lemon — the tea tree brings a mental clearing, the lemon makes thought bright and clear without turning sharp.",
    "dailyPractice": "Spend five minutes writing down a fact you've been avoiding. Don't judge what you wrote; just look at it. Then write underneath: \"I see you, and I can carry you forward with me.\"",
    "awarenessNote": "Truth is like a mirror just wiped clean — it shows every line and every mark on your face. You can be disappointed by that, or you can know yourself better through it. A mirror isn't there to make you perfect; it's there to show you what's real. Your response to what's real is what decides everything.",
