    "keywords": "Learning, practicality, focus, a grounded start, committing seriously",
    "uprightMessage": "The coin in your hand isn't a symbol of wealth but of the thing you're learning. You examine it seriously, like studying the facets of a gem. That grounded willingness to learn is your greatest resource — talent may carry you somewhere, and this step-by-step patience can carry you anywhere.",
    "reversedReminder": "What's keeping you from the first step? Can you name the fear? Not a vague \"fear of failing\", but specifically — seen by whom? Afraid of what happening? Once fear has a name it stops being enormous.",
    "symbolReading": "The page stands in green grass, holding a golden coin in both hands and gazing up at it as if in conversation. Earth within earth doubles the groundedness; his feet are firmly in the soil. Behind him lie freshly ploughed fields and low hills — everything at its beginning, and the soil is ready. His expression isn't excitement but attention.",
    "jungianAnalysis": "The apprentice archetype shows the power of beginner's mind — admitting you don't know, then learning seriously. His humility is genuine, not performed. His shadow is Mimulus's named fear — of being laughed at for speaking, of getting it wrong, of a visible, specific failure. Individuation begins with setting out carrying the fear, rather than waiting for the fear to leave.",
    "flowerSpectrum": "When you know exactly what you're afraid of and can't say it, and your limbs go weak in front of a concrete challenge, Mimulus keeps you company as you walk gently alongside that known fear, one small step at a time.",
    "step1Status": "You may be facing something very specific — presenting, a first date, asking a question — knowing clearly what you fear, while that fear glues your feet to the floor.",
    "step2Allow": "I allow myself to set out afraid; courage isn't the absence of fear.",
    "step3Body": "Notice the soles of your feet and your lower legs. Fear stiffens or weakens the legs — standing, sway your weight gently left and right so your feet feel the ground supporting them again.",
    "breathing": "In for four, feeling the ground under your soles; out for four, letting your weight sink into the earth. Take in steadiness, release the tremble — like a young tree rooting in wind. Eight times.",
    "aromaGuide": "Apply MUNI ONE oil to your inner ankles and palms, letting an earthlike scent warm you from the extremities and remind you: the ground you're standing on is solid; you can take one step.",
    "dailyPractice": "Take the smallest possible step towards the thing you fear today — not completing it but touching it: open the file, dial the first three seconds of the call, stand in front of the door. Then tell yourself: look, I'm still here.",
    "awarenessNote": "Awareness is like finding the light switch in a dark room — fear is the dark, and you don't have to destroy the dark, only find the switch. It's within reach, and its name is \"I know what I'm afraid of\". Saying the fear's name is pressing the switch.",
